      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(-x)&=a(-x)^3+b(-x)^2+c(-x)+d\\\\P(-x)&=-ax^3+bx^2-cx+d\\\\-P(x)&=-ax^3-bx^2-cx-d.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $P$ is odd, $P(-x)=-P(x)$ for every real $x$. Comparing the coefficients of $x^2$ and the constant terms gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}b&=-b, & d&=-d\\\\b&=0, & d&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
